      "message": "There is a chance that descriptors are overwritten:\nLet\u0027s assume that \"hook_task\" was executing tx_stream_kicker(), and it reached the line 171.\n- config-\u003ekicker_running is 1.\n- config-\u003etx_in_progress is 1.\n\nAt this point, \"UART TX FIFO IRQ handler\" calls usb_written(), and queue_count(tx_q) is 511 (tx_q-\u003ebuffer_units_mask). usb_writte() eventually calls tx_stream_handler() and also reaches to line 171, and executes the rest of this function, setting TX endpoint descriptors.\n- config-\u003ekicker_running is 0.\n- config-\u003etx_in_progress is 1.\n\nThe control comes back to \"hook_task\", line 171, and executes the rest of this function, overwriting TX endpoint descriptors, which is likely to be busy with previous setting.",
